This seems a plenty good idea, though I think it should be something
everyone can do, depending on Int.

The problem with spells as they stood a couple of versions ago was that if
you found a good one, you were so very much better than if you hadn't, so the
game was much more luck-based. 

An idea Brad had, which should tie into this somehow, is to make spellbooks
work forever, in particular, NOT DISAPPEAR - but you have to carry them
around! (Or one way you can fail to cast is "You rip the book apart in your
frustration.") This is nice, because it restores the trade-off effect
that comes with tools (say).

